    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 1,"desk": "ai","entities": ["openai"],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "ai-wrgtbcw4st1ss2j9","lenses": ["chips","cyber","trade"],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T21:55:23Z","rank_score": 1.569934,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": "science","source_form": "article","source_id": "techcrunch-ai","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "TechCrunch - AI","source_url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/01/openai-might-rebrand-its-data-centers-as-ai-compute-campuses","summary": "Axios reports that OpenAI is preparing a public-relations campaign after the midterm elections, when Democrats may regain control of Congress. The company's chief global affairs officer Chris Lehane told Axios about several proposals, including rebranding data centers as 'AI compute campuses.' He described the surrounding debate as healthy and said communities should hold companies accountable for transformative benefits.","time_source": "feed","title": "OpenAI Plans Rebranding Data Centers as AI Compute Campuses","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "ai","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": true},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": ["incident"],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "ai-v2vvag0p2n5hg5s6","lenses": ["china","cyber","trade"],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T23:24:00Z","rank_score": 1.542703,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "straitstimes-business","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "The Straits Times","source_url": "https://straitstimes.com/business/binance-details-us3-6-billion-in-net-outflows-after-cyber-theft","summary": "Binance disclosed a net outflow of US$3.6 billion (S$4.6 billion) in cryptoassets after restoring customer withdrawals on Nov 1, describing it as a relatively soft blow amid the largest cyber theft ever, attributed to North Korean hackers and an employee\u2019s compromised laptop. Binance had frozen withdrawals following the Oct 29 US$6.3 billion hack and pledged full reimbursement. The company replaced about 95% of stolen cryptocurrency using its corporate treasury and emergency funds. With roughly US$171 billion in assets under management, experts praised its swift response while noting fresh concerns over crypto security as attacks on firms like Bitget rise.","time_source": "feed","title": "Binance Reports $3.6 Billion Outflow After Historic Hack","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "ai","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "ai-p0szqt7ka66bk7t0","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T21:00:00Z","rank_score": 1.49038,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "straitstimes-business","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "The Straits Times","source_url": "https://straitstimes.com/business/askst-jobs-my-boss-keeps-making-passive-aggressive-remarks-how-should-i-respond","summary": "Business correspondent Timothy Goh presents answers from two executive-search leaders about how employees should respond when their managers use sarcasm or indirect remarks. Michelle Koh of The Edge Partnership says workers should reply to the content rather than tone, asking calm neutral questions and keeping a written record if needed, escalating only where demeaning patterns emerge. David Leong of PeopleWorldwide Consulting adds that disarming passive aggression means making implicit meaning explicit while still respecting authority.","time_source": "feed","title": "Singapore experts advise on handling passive-aggressive bosses at work","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "ai","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "ai-wbsctfq0mr0nq1yh","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T23:24:22Z","rank_score": 1.162842,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "simon-willison","source_kind": "analysis","source_name": "Simon Willison","source_url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/1/delete-uv-lock-first","summary": "A developer using Python 3.15 reports recurring confusing dependency errors after switching from earlier versions, advising that if in doubt one should delete the uv.lock file. They explain most of their projects are libraries without a locked file, but running tooling can leave behind pins for dependencies lacking a compatible wheel. As an example they cite watchfiles==1.1.1 failing to build because Python 3.15 exceeds PyO3's maximum supported version (3.14), and note that deleting the lock file usually resolves it.","time_source": "feed","title": "Python developer's workaround for dependency build errors on Python 3.15","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "ai","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": ["deal"],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "business-economy-em0ee09d2wmf5mf5","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T23:34:49Z","rank_score": 1.196831,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "bbc-business","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "BBC - Business","source_url": "https://bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crpdgp4y017go?at_campaign=rss&at_medium=RSS","summary": "Buy Now Pay Later (BNPL) transactions have been subject to affordability checks since July, when the service became officially regulated. Lenders such as Klarna and Clearpay must now obtain regulator approval to operate, with stricter background checks on shoppers' ability to repay; failing a check can block purchases entirely. Tips from former Citizens Advice debt adviser Sara Williams suggest slowing purchases, avoiding high credit limits for multiple items, cancelling subscriptions, and contacting debt charities. The government-backed MoneyHelper website offers free advice tools.","time_source": "feed","title": "New Buy Now Pay Later Rules May Block Purchases","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "business-economy","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "business-economy-sg8m8c6x1bsmetdv","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T22:25:51Z","rank_score": 1.17099,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "bbc-business","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "BBC - Business","source_url": "https://bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwly0eev3m44o?at_campaign=rss&at_medium=RSS","summary": "As Americans prepare for crucial midterm elections that will decide control of Congress, surveys suggest rising prices are central to how voters may cast their ballots. BBC journalist Clive Myrie visited North Carolina ahead of Tuesday's polls and spoke with voters about the issue. A producer credited the report as video produced by Janet Heaney and Davy McIlveen.","time_source": "feed","title": "Cost of living tops US midterm voter concerns","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "business-economy","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": ["openai"],"events": ["incident"],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "world-14nzb7w5z1qgj9qd","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T22:37:36Z","rank_score": 1.675312,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "guardian-world","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "The Guardian - World","source_url": "https://theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/01/chatgpt-woman-seizure-lawsuit-openai","summary": "Bowen Wan, a 31-year-old software engineer in Seattle, died of an epileptic seizure on 12 February this year after following advice from the chatbot ChatGPT. Her parents say she reduced her anti-seizure medication Lamotrigine from 400mg to zero based on that guidance and then died; they found her dead on 14 February, according to the lawsuit filed earlier this week against OpenAI. Wan's parents seek damages and an end to unlicensed medical advice by AI.","time_source": "feed","title": "Parents Sue OpenAI After ChatGPT Advice Tied to Woman's Death","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "world","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": true},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "medium","band_reason": "hedge_dropped","carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "world-r903t9sdf68856sq","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T23:05:05Z","rank_score": 1.18555,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "guardian-world","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "The Guardian - World","source_url": "https://theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/02/nationals-leader-matt-canavan-one-nation-james-ashby-capricornia-election-ntwnfb","summary": "Nationals leader Matt Canavan announced he will run in a lower house Queensland seat at the next federal election, potentially facing One Nation's James Ashby. The move follows Capricornia MP Michelle Landry's retirement and comes as Canavan faces pressure over his Senate position if polls remain strong for One Nation under Pauline Hanson.","time_source": "feed","title": "Canavan to contest Queensland seat amid One Nation rivalry","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "world","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "world-qzk15jx273zppmyb","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T22:30:00Z","rank_score": 1.172513,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "npr-world","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "NPR - World","source_url": "https://npr.org/2026/11/01/nx-s1-6025438/this-legendary-board-game-could-take-decades-to-complete","summary": "Andy Taeger and James Purcell are attempting to become the first people ever to complete Campaign for North Africa, described as one of the most complex board games in existence. The game is so intricate that finishing it could take decades.","time_source": "feed","title": "Two players aim to finish a decades-long board game","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "world","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 1,"desk": "world","entities": [],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "world-9qqw0956c1svk4vk","lenses": ["war"],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T22:19:13Z","rank_score": 1.168564,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "npr-world","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "NPR - World","source_url": "https://npr.org/2026/11/01/nx-s1-6023237/gulf-leaders-meet-in-qatar-in-effort-to-stave-off-new-escalation-in-u-s-and-iran-war","summary": "Qatar has led intense mediation over the past 72 hours to prevent a new round of possible U.S. attacks on Iran following Tuesday's midterm elections. The uncertainty has placed the entire Gulf region on edge, with leaders gathering to stave off further escalation in the conflict.","time_source": "feed","title": "Gulf Leaders Meet in Qatar Amid U.S.-Iran Tensions","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "world","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": ["incident"],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "world-k8f30e724ehyvc21","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T21:55:01Z","rank_score": 1.159802,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "bbc-world","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "BBC - World","source_url": "https://bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c64g1y90p71eo?at_campaign=rss&at_medium=RSS","summary": "A rare humanitarian ceasefire in Kherson region has ended after allowing civilians to evacuate the occupied city of Oleshky, having been due to finish at 22:59 Ukrainian time on Sunday. Overnight strikes hit energy infrastructure across four regions, leaving hundreds of thousands of homes without power and killing two people including a 13-year-old girl in Vinnytsia region. President Zelensky said strike intensity had been extremely high over the past week as Russia sought to exploit shortages of interceptors while Ukraine requested more Patriot missiles.","time_source": "feed","title": "Ceasefire Ends as Russian Strikes Leave Thousands Without Power in Ukraine","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "world","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "low","band_reason": "faithfulness","carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "world-hfkx2tcahqyhg93r","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T23:14:59Z","rank_score": 1.159282,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "cna-world","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "CNA","source_url": "https://channelnewsasia.com/women/breast-cancer-chemotherapy-running-single-mum-6461851","summary": "Cassandra Hie, a 53-year-old single mother in Singapore, kept running through breast cancer and chemotherapy. Chemotherapy left her feet too swollen to wear shoes, so she ran barefoot on the Kallang Park Connector. She drew on her eyebrows during runs after chemo removed them. Running eased nausea from treatment. Her journey began in 2015 during a divorce; she chose running for its convenience and low cost. Diagnosed with Stage Two breast cancer in April 2019, she finished the 55km Vietnam Jungle Marathon before surgery. She ran through all five months of chemotherapy despite her doctor warning against long-distance running. Since treatment, Hie has placed among the top three in more than 10 competitions and was first female overall in a 50km race in Malaysia in 2025. \u201cRunning saved my life,\u201d she said.","time_source": "feed","title": "Breast cancer survivor runs barefoot through treatment, credits running with saving her life","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "world","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "medium","band_reason": "faithfulness","carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "world-f6fy4ntpt9bgrw42","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T23:06:19Z","rank_score": 1.156014,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "cna-world","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "CNA","source_url": "https://channelnewsasia.com/sport/list-formula-one-world-champions-6511671","summary": "A list of Formula One world champions shows Kimi Antonelli winning his first title in Mexico City on Sunday, dated November. He took the crown with Mercedes, ending a run dominated by Verstappen and Hamilton across earlier seasons.","time_source": "feed","title": "Kimi Antonelli becomes first Formula One champion of 2026","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "world","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "medium","band_reason": "hedge_dropped","carried_by": 1,"desk": "world","entities": [],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "world-dkzqwky7m59gg64r","lenses": ["war"],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T23:00:00Z","rank_score": 1.153643,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "japan-times","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "The Japan Times","source_url": "https://japantimes.co.jp/culture/2026/11/02/film/in-their-traces","summary": "Shigeru Kobayashi\u2019s documentary \u2018In Their Traces\u2019 follows female survivors of sexual violence, prompting viewers to question whether a veteran male director in his 70s is suited to the subject. In production notes, Kobayashi admits he shared those misgivings himself, and addresses them directly \u2014 an approach the film\u2019s maker has called his last major work that makes it resonate.","time_source": "feed","title": "Veteran Director Reflects on Filming Survivors\u2019 Stories","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "world","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 1,"desk": null,"entities": ["rbi"],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "india-f0y2m9gstaqve6bv","lenses": ["cyber"],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T19:06:31Z","rank_score": 1.572421,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "economic-times","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "The Economic Times","source_url": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/india/crypto-cards-enter-rbis-radar-as-indians-use-offshore-wallets-for-everyday-payments/articleshow/135436233.cms","summary": "Crypto debit cards accessed through international providers like RedotPay have drawn attention from the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) and Financial Intelligence Unit (FIU), two persons told ET. Several Indian residents' access to pre-paid crypto cards has been blocked recently, and no confirmation was available from payment firms or the central bank. The non-profit Digital South Trust submitted findings on stablecoin-based offshore card programmes used for everyday payments in India. Legal experts say such arrangements may violate FEMA regulations because foreign custodian accounts convert cryptocurrency into fiat currency automatically.","time_source": "feed","title": "RBI and FIU probe offshore crypto cards used in India","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "india","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": true},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 2,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "india-0n4t94b71gc27rqv","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T21:30:55Z","rank_score": 1.31121,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "toi-india","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "Times of India - India","source_url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/introspect-on-need-to-improve-judiciary-responsiveness-cji/articleshow/135437999.cms","summary": "Chief Justice of India Surya Kant, speaking at the Kerala High Court's platinum jubilee celebration in New Delhi, urged constitutional courts to introspect and improve responsiveness. He emphasised that justice depends not only on final judgements but also on timely intervention when most needed. Highlighting Article 226 as a strength of judicial architecture, he questioned how urgent matters could be identified more effectively and whether listing procedures might become more transparent and predictable.","time_source": "feed","title": "CJI Calls for Judicial Self-Reflection on Court Responsiveness","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "india","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false},
    {"also_covered_by": null,"also_ran_earlier": [],"band": "high","band_reason": null,"carried_by": 2,"desk": null,"entities": [],"events": [],"introduced_by_run": 1,"item_id": "india-8kd187jc9dw8ktjn","lenses": [],"on_front_page": false,"published_at": "2026-11-01T21:20:21Z","rank_score": 1.307484,"reader_note": null,"same_story_as": null,"secondary_desk": null,"source_form": "article","source_id": "toi-india","source_kind": "reporting","source_name": "Times of India - India","source_url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/poverty-removal-not-just-slogan-pm-modi-on-world-bank-data/articleshow/135437969.cms","summary": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi said on Saturday that India recorded one of the world's fastest poverty declines, with extreme poverty collapsing by 90% between 2011 and 2023 to a low of 2. 6%. He cited World Bank figures stating nearly 50 crore people moved out of poverty over those years, employment grew by 13. 4 crore from 2017 to 2023, and the Gini index fell over 20% from 29 in 2011 to 23 in 2023. Modi called elimination of poverty a government commitment rather than slogan.","time_source": "feed","title": "Modi Credits World Bank Data for India's Poverty Decline","truncated": false,"updated_at": null,"updated_by_run": null,"vertical": "india","visual": null,"watchlist_hit": false}
